    title_en: "South Korea's Ministry of Foreign Affairs Online Education System Breached: Attackers Used Zero-Day Vulnerability and Configuration Flaws to Exfiltrate Diplomatic Personnel Data for Extended Period",
    summary_en: "The Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MOFA) of South Korea issued a press release on July 20, revealing that its affiliated National Diplomatic Academy (KNDA) online education system was subjected to a cyberattack. Attackers exploited a zero-day vulnerability in the system server software, combined with system security configuration deficiencies, to gain server control and continuously access the system from April 2025 to February 2026, maintaining access for nearly ten months. This system is primarily used for professional and language training courses for diplomatic personnel. Although MOFA stated that the specific leaked content is currently difficult to confirm, the system contained educational data such as the names and accounts of trainees. Due to the security vulnerabilities and management deficiencies, the data was exposed to risk for an extended period. MOFA has urgently shut down the system and is continuing the investigation, promising to cooperate with relevant agencies to continuously improve internal security systems and management measures to prevent similar incidents in the future.",
    tags_en: ["Ministry of Foreign Affairs", "KNDA", "Zero-Day Vulnerability", "Data Leakage", "Cyberattack", "Education System"],
