    title_en: "FBI Warns: Scammers Impersonating Law Enforcement to Lure Victims into Providing Personal Data via 'Fund Recovery'",
    summary_en: "The U.S. Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI), through its Internet Crime Complaint Center (IC3), has issued a warning that scammers are exploiting victims' urgent desire to recover lost funds by conducting 'fund recovery scams,' also known as 'double scams.' Scammers contact victims who have been defrauded via email, phone calls, social media (such as Facebook Messenger), or by creating fake accounts. They demand that victims click malicious links to update their complaint information, or guide victims to fake IC3 websites to fill out personal data. More advanced scams even utilize AI technology to create deepfake videos of high-ranking FBI officials to deceive victims. IC3 emphasizes that official personnel will not proactively contact complainants through any communication software, nor will they ever request victims to pay any fees to recover lost funds. The public must always directly enter the official website www.ic3.gov and remain vigilant, avoiding clicking on unknown links or websites.",
    tags_en: ["FBI", "IC3", "Scam", "Deepfake", "Cybercrime", "Personal Data Theft"],
