    category: "Linux",
    title: "Canonical 公布三項 Ubuntu Snap 漏洞：包含可升權特權與存取密碼雜湊值",
    summary: "Canonical 近期揭露了三項影響 snapd 的安全漏洞。其中，CVE-2026-8933 允許本地攻擊者提升權限，影響追溯至 Ubuntu 22.04 的 LTS 版本，評級為高風險。另一高風險漏洞 CVE-2026-15226 則允許本地攻擊者逃脫 Snap 的限制環境，從受限根目錄進入未受限根目錄。此外，CVE-2024-5300 是一個影響追溯至 Ubuntu 16.04 LTS 的漏洞，允許沙盒應用程式存取雜湊形式的用戶密碼。這些漏洞皆涉及 Ubuntu 的 Snap 應用程式生態系統，實務上要求用戶及系統管理員應儘速更新 snapd 及相關系統元件，以修補這些潛在的權限提升與資料洩漏風險。",
    tags: ["Ubuntu", "Snap", "snapd", "CVE-2026-8933", "CVE-2026-15226", "CVE-2024-5300", "Canonical"],
    title_en: "Canonical Discloses Three Ubuntu Snap Vulnerabilities: Including Privilege Escalation and Password Hash Access",
    summary_en: "Canonical recently disclosed three security vulnerabilities affecting snapd. Among them, CVE-2026-8933 allows a local attacker to escalate privileges, affecting Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, and is rated as high risk. Another high-risk vulnerability, CVE-2026-15226, allows a local attacker to escape the Snap's restricted environment, moving from a restricted root directory to an unrestricted one. Furthermore, CVE-2024-5300 is a vulnerability affecting Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, which allows sandbox applications to access hashed user passwords. These vulnerabilities all involve the Ubuntu Snap application ecosystem, practically requiring users and system administrators to promptly update snapd and related system components to patch these potential privilege escalation and data leakage risks.",
    tags_en: ["Ubuntu", "Snap", "snapd", "CVE-2026-8933", "CVE-2026-15226", "CVE-2024-5300", "Canonical"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Phoronix", url: "https://phoronix.com/news/Ubuntu-Snap-Three-More-Vulns", lang: "EN" }
    ]
