    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "研究揭示雲端租戶可利用 GPU 運算負荷，在無漏洞情況下威脅電網穩定性",
    summary: "研究人員提出 Bit2Watt 攻擊模型，指出雲端租戶僅透過運算工作負載的電力波動，即可在不需任何漏洞或入侵的情況下，對資料中心所連接的電網造成威脅。該技術利用 GPU 運算時的功耗特性，透過週期性地在高強度運算和低功耗狀態間切換，產生可控的電力振盪。攻擊方法包括 SWMA（上傳專用 CUDA kernel）和 LTMA（將調變隱藏於真實 LLM 訓練流程中），後者更難被偵測。在模擬的 1 MW 本地電網情境下，當 1,000 個 GPU 同步調變時，總諧波失真（THD）可達 46.8%，遠超標準，且阻尼比可能變成負值，導致電網放大擾動。此風險強調了純粹的計算行為作為合法工作負載，如何被武器化來破壞電力基礎設施的潛在威脅。",
    tags: ["Bit2Watt", "GPU", "電力網格", "雲端運算", "CUDA", "OT/ICS"],
    title_en: "Research Reveals Cloud Tenants Can Threaten Grid Stability Using GPU Computational Load, Even Without Vulnerabilities",
    summary_en: "Researchers proposed the Bit2Watt attack model, pointing out that cloud tenants can threaten the power grid connected to a data center merely through power fluctuations from computational workloads, without needing any vulnerabilities or intrusions. This technique utilizes the power consumption characteristics of GPU computation, generating controllable power oscillations by cyclically switching between high-intensity computation and low-power states. Attack methods include SWMA (uploading dedicated CUDA kernels) and LTMA (hiding modulation within real LLM training processes), the latter being harder to detect. In a simulated 1 MW local grid scenario, when 1,000 GPUs modulate synchronously, the total harmonic distortion (THD) can reach 46.8%, far exceeding standards, and the damping ratio may become negative, leading to grid-amplified disturbances. This risk highlights the potential threat of pure computational behavior, as a legitimate workload, being weaponized to disrupt power infrastructure.",
    tags_en: ["Bit2Watt", "GPU", "Power Grid", "Cloud Computing", "CUDA", "OT/ICS"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Hacker News", url: "https://thehackernews.com/2026/07/new-bit2watt-attack-could-let-cloud.html", lang: "EN" }
    ]
