    title: "Google Chrome Android 存在 ANGLE 越界讀寫漏洞，可能導致沙盒逃逸",
    summary: "本漏洞為 CVE-2026-16419，存在於 Google Chrome 瀏覽器在 Android 平台上的 ANGLE 渲染元件。該漏洞屬於越界讀寫（Out of bounds read and write），若攻擊者透過精心構造的 HTML 網頁，可能成功執行沙盒逃逸（sandbox escape）。這類漏洞的嚴重性被評定為高風險（High）。受影響的產品版本為 Android 平台，且版本號早於 150.0.7871.182。實務上，攻擊者可利用此漏洞在遠端執行程式碼，繞過瀏覽器的安全沙盒機制。修補建議是立即更新 Google Chrome 瀏覽器至 150.0.7871.182 或更高版本，以修補 ANGLE 渲染元件的缺陷。",
    tags: ["Google Chrome", "Android", "CVE-2026-16419", "ANGLE", "越界讀寫", "沙盒逃逸"],
    title_en: "Google Chrome Android has ANGLE out-of-bounds read/write vulnerability, potentially leading to sandbox escape",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability, CVE-2026-16419, exists in the ANGLE rendering component of the Google Chrome browser on the Android platform. The vulnerability is an out-of-bounds read and write flaw. If an attacker uses a specially crafted HTML webpage, they may successfully achieve a sandbox escape. The severity of this vulnerability is rated as High risk. The affected product version is the Android platform, specifically versions earlier than 150.0.7871.182. In practice, attackers can exploit this vulnerability to execute code remotely, bypassing the browser's security sandbox mechanism. The recommended fix is to immediately update Google Chrome browser to version 150.0.7871.182 or later, to patch the defect in the ANGLE rendering component.",
