    title_en: "Google Releases Gemini 3.6 Flash and 3.5 Flash-Lite, and Launches Dedicated Model to Assist in Finding and Fixing Security Vulnerabilities",
    summary_en: "Google recently announced the launch of several new generations of Gemini models, including Gemini 3.6 Flash, Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite, and Gemini 3.5 Flash Cyber, which is specifically designed for security applications. Compared to its predecessor, Gemini 3.6 Flash has improved 'Token efficiency' and demonstrates more reliable performance in code generation, such as showing a 49% improvement in DeepSWE testing (compared to 37%). Furthermore, its knowledge cutoff date has been updated from January 2025 to March 2026. Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite is designed for high-throughput, low-latency tasks, demonstrating excellent performance in agentic search and document processing. Notably, Google has introduced Gemini 3.5 Flash Cyber, a tool specifically used for finding and fixing code security vulnerabilities. This is implemented via CodeMender and will initially be offered to government entities and trusted partners through a limited access pilot program. The release of these models indicates that Google is deeply integrating AI capabilities into the software development and security defense processes, providing more efficient vulnerability detection and remediation capabilities for the front lines of cybersecurity defense.",
    tags_en: ["Google", "Gemini 3.6 Flash", "Gemini 3.5 Flash Cyber", "AI Model", "Security Vulnerability", "CodeMender"],
