    summary_en: "This article discusses trends in the wearable device market, noting that while the Apple Watch is highly functional, its daily charging requirement and constant notification interruptions lead some users to seek health tracking devices that are less intrusive and focus more on background data collection. To address this, Garmin has launched the CIRQA smart band, a smart band that uniquely emphasizes a 'screenless' experience. It is designed to track advanced fitness and health features without requiring a subscription service. The band's biggest advantage is its long battery life of up to 10 days, providing continuous health and fitness monitoring data that users can access in real-time via the Garmin Connect application. Furthermore, the market also includes devices like the Oura ring and fitness bands from Fitbit and Whoop, collectively driving the growth of this 'low-intrusion' wearable category. This suggests that Apple may need to consider expanding its product line beyond the Apple Watch to include devices like smart rings or smart bands that are better suited for background monitoring.",
