    category: "重點關注",
    title: "法院批准 Anthropic 15 億美元著作權和解案：涉及 AI 訓練資料的著作權爭議",
    summary: "本案涉及 AI 公司 Anthropic 與多位作者之間的著作權集體訴訟。法院此前已裁定 Anthropic 使用書籍進行 AI 訓練屬於合理使用（fair use），但其盜用作品的行為可能不屬於合理使用。最終，法官批准了總額達 15 億美元的和解方案，這被稱為有史以來最大的著作權和解。儘管部分作者最初對和解金額和律師費用提出異議，但法官強調了高參與率，認為大多數作者接受了該方案。法官最終大幅削減了原先律師要求的費用比例，將原本的 12.5% 降至約 7%，總費用約為 1.01 億美元。此案對於 AI 訓練資料的合法性、著作權邊界劃定，以及大型科技公司與創作者權益的平衡，具有重大的實務意義。",
    tags: ["Anthropic", "著作權", "AI 訓練資料", "集體訴訟", "合理使用", "法律議題"],
    title_en: "Court Approves $1.5 Billion Copyright Settlement for Anthropic: Addressing Copyright Disputes in AI Training Data",
    summary_en: "This case involves a class-action lawsuit between the AI company Anthropic and multiple authors. The court had previously ruled that Anthropic's use of books for AI training constituted fair use, but the court suggested that the act of misappropriating works might not fall under fair use. Ultimately, the judge approved a settlement totaling $1.5 billion, described as the largest copyright settlement to date. Although some authors initially objected to the settlement amount and legal fees, the judge emphasized the high participation rate, noting that most authors accepted the proposal. The judge subsequently significantly reduced the percentage of fees originally requested by the lawyers, lowering it from 12.5% to approximately 7%, resulting in total costs of about $101 million. This case holds significant practical implications for the legality of AI training data, the delineation of copyright boundaries, and the balance of rights between large technology companies and creators.",
    tags_en: ["Anthropic", "Copyright", "AI Training Data", "Class Action Lawsuit", "Fair Use", "Legal Issues"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Ars Technica", url: "https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/07/judge-approves-anthropics-1-5-billion-copyright-settlement-with-authors", lang: "EN" }
    ]
