    title_en: "Steam Deck Sales Data Analysis: Steep Decline in Sales After Price Hike, Market Performance Below Expectations",
    summary_en: "This article analyzes the changing sales trends of the Steam Deck since its launch in 2022. According to data analysis from the Linux gaming website Boiling Steam, the sales of the handheld gaming computer showed a noticeable decline after a price increase in May. The data shows that the Steam Deck's ranking dropped from 5th place in May to 14th place in July, indicating market performance below previous levels. Rough estimates suggest that sales may have dropped significantly from a baseline of approximately 11,000 to 18,000 units per week in 2025, down to only 1,400 to 3,000 units per week. This represents a massive slowdown in the handheld console's sales velocity. Although the article does not provide specific vulnerabilities or security information, it reveals a significant trend change in product market sales, reminding developers and players to pay attention to the market acceptance and the impact of pricing strategy on sales for hardware products.",
