    summary_en: "In this announcement, Google unveiled a major update to its AI model suite, introducing Gemini 3.6 Flash to replace the previously popular 3.5 Flash. This model has been optimized based on user feedback, significantly improving code generation capabilities, raising the score in DeepSWE tests from 3.5 Flash's 37% to 49%. Furthermore, Google launched new versions, including Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite and Gemini 3.5 Flash Cyber. While enhancing performance, 3.6 Flash has significantly reduced energy consumption, decreasing usage by approximately 17%, and lowering API costs to $1.50/1M input tokens and $7.50/1M output tokens. Flash Lite is positioned as a highly efficient solution for agentic systems at a price of $0.30/1M input tokens. These updates aim to make AI models more cost-effective and improve accuracy in complex workflows.",
