    title: "TreeSize 轉向訂閱制：原購買者若未續訂，將面臨無法獲取更新與安裝檔的困境",
    summary: "磁碟空間分析工具 TreeSize 的開發商 JAM Software，正逐步將其產品線轉向訂閱模式。對於購買了永久授權（perpetual license）的用戶，一旦維護期結束，若不續訂訂閱，將無法獲得更新、技術支援，甚至無法取得安裝程式或授權金鑰。開發商指出，此舉是為了在當前經濟環境下，確保長期可靠的產品開發與支援。用戶反饋指出，這讓已付費的客戶失去了下載其已擁有版本安裝檔的權利。JAM Software 方面表示，在支援期結束後，他們不會永久保留所有舊版安裝檔和金鑰，以避免舊版軟體可能包含已知的錯誤或安全漏洞。用戶應留意其授權的維護期到期日，並主動進行資料備份。",
    tags: ["TreeSize", "JAM Software", "訂閱制", "永久授權", "軟體支援", "資安漏洞"],
    title_en: "TreeSize shifts to subscription model: Original purchasers may face difficulties accessing updates and installers if they do not renew",
    summary_en: "JAM Software, the developer of the disk space analysis tool TreeSize, is gradually transitioning its product line to a subscription model. For users who purchased a perpetual license, once the maintenance period ends and the subscription is not renewed, they will be unable to receive updates, technical support, or even obtain the installer or license key. The developer stated that this move is necessary to ensure long-term, reliable product development and support in the current economic climate. User feedback indicates that this deprives paying customers of the right to download installers for versions they already own. JAM Software stated that after the support period ends, they will not permanently retain all old version installers and keys, in order to prevent old software from potentially containing known errors or security vulnerabilities. Users should pay attention to their license maintenance expiration date and proactively perform data backups.",
    tags_en: ["TreeSize", "JAM Software", "Subscription Model", "Perpetual License", "Software Support", "Security Vulnerability"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Ars Technica", url: "https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/07/treesize-wont-renew-perpetual-license-support-unless-users-subscribe", lang: "EN" }
    ]
